00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.800
You practiced it a lot!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.350
It will be okay!

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.060
Y-You can do it! Calm down, Honoka!

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.940
All you have to do is be yourself
during the practical test!

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.440
But that's the hardest part!

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:25.580
That place seemed
like a totally different world.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.880
Whoa!

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.380
Amazing!

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.560
The National Magic University
Affiliated First High School.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:45.480
The 2095 entrance exams.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.110
The one who got the top scores
was this girl... Miyuki Shiba.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:57.240
{=0}MATRICULATION CEREMONY

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:58.570
As mild sunshine streams in
and vivid cherry blossoms float in the air

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.370
on this gorgeous spring day...

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:07.250
being able to enroll at National Magic
University Affiliated First High School...

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:12.210
fills me with great joy, as well as honor.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:12.210
So, that girl's one of the people
you said caught your eye?

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:17.130
Yes. I wish you could've seen her, too, Shizuku!
You wouldn't believe how cool she was!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.640
Is that right?

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.600
All right, it's settled! I'm going to be
friends with Ms. Shiba, no matter what!

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:27.980
...as a student of this prestigious school...

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.980
"Equally, cohesively, and in matters
other than magic, as well," huh?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.400
She's doing a great job weaving
those rigid phrases into her speech.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:40.370
You have that evil look
on your face again, President.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.490
She's exactly what I was hoping for!

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.220
"Nice to meet you.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:00.340
I'm Honoka Mitsui!
I hope we can be friends!"

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:06.270
No, no! That's too casual! Okay.
"Good afternoon, my name is Honoka Mitsui.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.520
I am pleased to make your acquaintance."

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.190
That was kind of stiff, huh?

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:14.780
Hey, Shizuku, which introduction will
leave the best impression on her?

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.950
Any one will do,
but here she comes. Ms. Shiba.

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.780
Whoa, she's here!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:20.780
Hey! It's Ms. Shiba!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.660
So cute!

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.580
Good morning.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.250
She's like a goddess!
I'd love to get closer to her!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.460
Hey, Ms. Shiba's seat is behind me.

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.500
Huh? Huh? H-Hey,
you should've told me that sooner!

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.260
Sorry. I only noticed now.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:41.590
I-I have to come up with a tasteful greeting!
"That hair ornament is so lovely!" Like that?

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.470
No, I'm not hitting on her!
How about, "I'm a big fan"?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.930
No, that doesn't make any sense, either!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.400
Go on, it's your chance
to introduce yourself. You can do it.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.240
Right! It's now or never!
You've got this, Honoka! Go for it!

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.200
Oh, um, Ms. Shiba--

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.450
What was that? Is she okay?

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.210
Who knew we had such a klutz in our class?

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:14.540
M-My whole high school life is over.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.550
Are you all right?

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:24.970
Oh, thank you.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.600
You're welcome. Um...

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.560
M-My name is Mitsui! Honoka Mitsui!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.310
I'm Miyuki Shiba.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.980
Let's be friends, shall we, Ms. Mitsui?

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.900
I-I'd like that, too.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.320
All's well that ends well!
You did it, Honoka!

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.860
Please excuse her, Ms. Shiba.
She's a really ditzy girl.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:47.870
Hey, that's harsh, Shizuku! Well, I admit
that I did kind of make a fool of myself.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.870
Excuse me, and who's your friend?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:53.250
I'm Shizuku Kitayama.
I've already heard a lot about you...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.420
since Honoka's a huge fan of yours.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.590
Hey! Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:01.920
Excuse me. Have we already
met somewhere before?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.800
She saw you at the test venue,
and it was love at first sight--

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.140
Hey, enough! You're embarrassing me!
Shizuku, you dummy!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.390
Are you having lunch
in the cafeteria, too, Ms. Shiba?

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:17.060
Yes. May I join you?

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:20.940
Of course! We should be
the ones asking you in fact!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.700
Oh no, the place is packed.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.870
Are there any empty seats?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.290
Oh! Who's that?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.920
Hey, you guys...

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.210
Mind giving up those seats?

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.340
Huh?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:47.590
You Course 2 students are just our reserves.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.300
Whether we're in class or in the cafeteria,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:54.350
you should give up your seats for
any Course 1 student, no questions asked!

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:55.520
Excuse me...

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.730
Fine.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.940
I'm done eating, so I'm heading out.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.280
H-Hey, Tatsuya!

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.070
Tatsuya!

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.780
This is ridiculous. Let's go, too.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.540
Yeah.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.120
That's the right attitude!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.540
All right, Ms. Shiba,
these seats are yours now.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.040
But I...

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.840
After all, Course 2 students are Weeds!
In other words, they're inferior!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.880
That's pretty disrespectful of you to eat
at the same place with us Course 1 students.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.430
Don't you all agree?

00:07:26.430 --> 00:07:27.590
That's right!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.470
Know your place, loser Weeds!

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.180
No way.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.930
Oh, Ms. Shiba!

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.490
I'm so sorry for making a scene.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.530
Oh, please.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:51.080
So, he's a Course 2 student.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.280
What if he is?

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.700
That's weird. I was positive
he was a Course 1 student!

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.040
What?

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:02.630
See, there was one other person besides
you who caught my eye during the exams.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.550
Normally, you'll see the byproducts of your
magic sequence in the form of light waves,

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.600
but there wasn't a
single trace with that student.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:18.810
So, you may have devastating
magic power, Ms. Shiba...

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:24.440
but it seems like he's only using
the bare minimum of his magic power.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.190
Anyway, it was such gorgeous magic!

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.570
It really must've been,
for you to gush about it.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:32.320
Hmm... Come to think of it...

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.790
Right! I'm a Mitsui, so I'm more sensitive
to light oscillation than most!

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:42.630
But who would've thought a Course 2
student could cast such gorgeous spells?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.250
Thank you so much...

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.260
Ms. Mitsui!

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.380
What?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.090
Whaaat?

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.510
That boy is your big brother?

00:08:54.510 --> 00:09:00.440
Talented magicians who happen to be siblings...
But her big brother's a Course 2 student, huh?

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.400
Really, enough already!

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.200
Didn't you hear Miyuki say
that she's going home with her brother?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.370
There's something we need to discuss
with her as fellow Course 1 students!

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.040
Just back off, Course 2 student!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:17.950
What?

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:22.040
What gives you the right
to try to split those two apart?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.130
What? "Split us apart," did you say?

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:27.380
Oh, Mizuki, how you do misunderstand?

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.050
I'm gonna split you two apart!

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:31.970
Brother!

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.600
Miyuki!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:40.140
I'm never going to let go of you again, Miyuki.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.980
Please don't ever let go of me, Brother.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.770
Brother, please!

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.150
Miyuki?

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:54.950
Excuse me, Ms. Shiba,
but you're wrong about that.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.200
You may be siblings,
but a Weed is just a spare.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:01.000
We have to draw the line
between Course 1 and Course 2!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.380
At this school, there are
the honor students, the Blooms,

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:09.130
and the irregular students, the Weeds.
It's a clear distinction.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.260
It's an irrefutable fact.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:12.630
You all agree with me, right?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:15.300
That's right.
Ms. Shiba needs to hang with us.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.050
You losers can just back off!

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.310
But that's just terrible, you guys.

00:10:19.310 --> 00:10:20.430
Losers go home!

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:21.520
Get lost now!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.060
You are failures...

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.650
Being set apart
from her own brother by course...

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.650
Go home!

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:28.110
Ms. Shiba's the one
who's suffering the most!

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.320
But they can't even see that,

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.900
and they're looking down on the
Course 2 students in front of her.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.570
What's wrong with these people?

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:37.200
It makes me feel stupid
for being so proud of making Course 1!

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.950
Especially that guy! What was his name?
"Moriyama"? Could he be more clueless?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.040
This Magic High School runs on a meritocracy.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:46.460
Since you Weeds are inferior in talent,

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.920
that makes your very
existence inferior, as well.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.840
I think it's time you all learned your place.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:53.840
But we're all new students here!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:57.930
Just how much better than us
can you be at this stage?

00:10:57.930 --> 00:11:00.640
Don't talk like Blooms and Weeds are equal!

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.350
All right, why don't I show you
how much stronger we are?

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.180
Don't tell me...

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:06.480
You're going to cast an attack spell here?

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:30.960
Looks like the Course 2 student
just got the better of you, Mr. Course 1.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.880
No way can a Bloom ever fall behind a Weed!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.170
Don't give us that!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.500
Come on, enough of this--

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.930
Shut up!

00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.390
Honoka!

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.720
There's something wrong with you all!

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:47.690
All you're doing is making Ms. Shiba suffer!

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.070
What do you think you're doing?

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:54.780
That's right, you!
Show them the power of a Course 1 student!

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:56.900
Why don't you shut up!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.780
I'm going to use my magic to stop you all!

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:11.210
Please... just settle down, everyone!

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.640
Stop it right now!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.310
Student Council President Saegusa!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.230
Chairman of the Disciplinary
Committee, Watanabe!

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:33.150
You there, the Class 1-A girl!

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.070
Oh, yes?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:38.070
You were just about to unleash
an attack spell, weren't you?

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:41.280
Except for self-defense, anti-personnel attacks
are not only against this school's rules,

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.780
they're also against the law.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.200
Huh? Um, actually...

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.210
I'd particularly like to hear
what you have to say.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.580
Please report
to the Disciplinary Committee Room.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.290
B-But...

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.500
in the end, I only made it worse.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.300
I even caused trouble
for the Student Council president.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.840
Honoka...

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.850
Why couldn't I have been more calm?

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:06.270
Now, I can never look Ms. Shiba in the eye!

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.480
I just know she hates me now!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.690
Please hold on a minute...

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.440
Disciplinary Committee Chairman.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:24.030
All she was about to unleash
was a Flash Spell, nothing more.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.200
I don't believe
there was any intent to attack.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:32.000
Oh? Do you mean you have the ability to read
activation sequences as they're being launched?

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.000
I'm no good at practical skills...

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.210
but I am adept at analysis.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.300
In that split second?

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.130
He's bluffing!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:40.590
Don't be stupid!

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.680
No way could he pull that off!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:48.220
Is Ms. Shiba's brother defending me?

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.560
Ms. Mitsui...

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.480
U-Um...

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.560
I-I...

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.400
You don't have to tell me.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:04.240
You weren't trying to attack just now.
You were trying to stop everyone, right?

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:11.410
But this is...

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.870
Our little secret, okay?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.250
Miyuki...

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.420
We've reached an understanding.

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.760
She has nothing to worry about, either.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.470
U-Um, excuse me... Uh...

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:31.680
I have to thank him properly! Why am
I at a loss for words at a time like this?

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:35.060
Thank you for defending Honoka.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:38.520
Thanks to you,
it didn't escalate into anything serious.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.320
Shizuku...

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:43.240
U-Um...

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.240
I'm sorry for what just happened, Big Brother!

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.080
It was no big deal.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:52.410
And don't call me "Big Brother," okay?
We're both first years here, right?

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.330
R-Right!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:55.920
Oh, wow!

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:59.090
So, there are Course 1 students
like her, too, huh?

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:08.470
Thank you for today!
You came to my rescue yet again, Shizuku!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.180
Aren't you glad you were able
to let them know how you feel?

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:15.310
Yes. But really, can you believe
how amazing the Course 2 students are, too?

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:19.270
That Erika girl sure was incredible, and
Ms. Shiba's brother was the most amazing of all.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.980
Identifying the magic behind
a launched activation sequence

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.990
is not something you can normally do.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:26.700
So, how can he be in Course 2?

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:30.950
What's the difference
between Courses 1 and 2 exactly?

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:35.410
"NATIONAL MAGIC UNIVERSITY
AFFILIATED FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:43.920
Ms. Shiba! Big Brother! Good morning!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.760
Good morning!

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.050
Didn't I tell you yesterday?
Don't call me "Big Brother."

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:51.430
Right. But what should I call you, then?

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:52.770
You can call me Tatsuya.

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.890
T-T-Tatsu... Tatsuya--

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:57.940
Tatsuya!

00:15:57.940 --> 00:16:02.650
Ta-tsu-ya!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.280
What's going on,
Student Council President?

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.370
Now, now...
Let's not stand on ceremony.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:16.870
You can just call me Mayumi, all right?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:18.830
Um, forgive me if I'm being rude,

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.800
but didn't you meet my brother for the
first time during the matriculation ceremony?

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:27.050
I wonder if that's true!
Could it be true?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.100
We've already met in the distant past.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:36.390
Split apart by a cruel twist of fate,
but once again drawn toward each other

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:39.900
until we were reunited
on the day of the matriculation ceremony!

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:42.770
Reunited at last, huh, Mayumi?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.780
Tatsuya...

00:16:47.530 --> 00:16:50.990
No! Brother, when did such a thing happen?

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:56.580
Just kidding! It's true that we met for the
first time during the matriculation ceremony.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.290
But...

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.460
Tatsuya, did you feel a sense of destiny?

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:04.920
If this is destiny,
then it's not fate, but rather doom.

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.840
Is that right? Crap.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.090
Enough is enough, you!

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:14.300
Just give them the message! Don't you have
something to say to the Shiba siblings?

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.220
Tell us something?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:20.690
I'd like to invite you two
to lunch in the Student Council Office.

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:24.820
That bizarre familiarity
she showed my brother...

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.280
It'd be risky to allow her to get close to him!

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:31.070
Hey, don't worry, I won't bite.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:36.410
It's just that, in order to make this academy
even better, I'd like to enlist your aid.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.700
You have your own opinion, don't you?

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.460
About this school.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:50.010
I wonder what the Student Council
president wanted.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.550
I think she's going to
invite them to join the council.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.850
Since traditionally,
the top new student always joins.

00:17:55.850 --> 00:17:59.220
Oh... Just what you'd expect of Ms. Shiba!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.730
But if that's the case,
then what about Tatsuya?

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:06.770
What? Tatsuya's joining
the Disciplinary Committee?

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:13.490
Why would a guy like that...

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:15.240
He's just a Weed!

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.500
It has to be his connection to Ms. Shiba!

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.630
Lucky him! Getting all this blatant special
treatment thanks to his talented sister...

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:30.300
Otherwise, a guy like him would never
get to be on the Disciplinary Committee.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:31.800
Not a loser Weed like him!

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:32.840
H-Hey!

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:33.220
Honoka!

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:34.930
But...

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:43.190
It wouldn't do any good to tell them
because they don't know

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:46.150
how good Tatsuya
and the other Course 2 students are.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:50.780
I feel so bitter. They're all so amazing.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:54.070
Why do people discriminate
between Course 1 and Course 2?

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.080
There's not much chance of getting
the current Course 1 students to understand.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:01.870
After all, you and I have
always believed it ourselves

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:06.540
that Course 1 is for the honor students,
and Course 2 is for the irregulars.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.670
You're right about that.

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:12.460
We were both so overjoyed
that we'd made Course 1.

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:14.970
But... But...

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:24.940
We already know all about
Tatsuya and the others' abilities.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:25.890
Huh?

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:30.860
It might not be possible to get everyone
to acknowledge them right away. So...

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:33.150
why don't we get things started?

00:19:33.150 --> 00:19:36.030
I mean, we're all First High students, right?

00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.240
Yeah.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:40.080
I'm so glad I got into this school!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:44.910
Because Tatsuya, Ms. Shiba
and everyone in Course 2 are all so talented!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.420
Well, after all,
we were your only rivals back home.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.710
The world is such a vast place, isn't it?

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:54.010
Let's work hard
so we can measure up to them!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.340
Yeah.

